  clock: 2  # 2d26
  nonce: 2d26  # 2d26
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\nCause holds: php.py _extract_laravel_routes still tests `arg_child.type == \"string\"` for the route path (now php.py:803). No commit since filing touched it (git log -S encapsed_string on php.py: last 686aa99c2c, 2026-04-15).\nLive repro (analyze_php on a 6-line scratch fixture): of Route::get(\"/users\",...), Route::post('/users',...), Route::match(['get','post'], \"/m\",...), Route::resource(\"photos\", PhotoController::class), Route::get(\"/u/{$x}\",...) ONLY the single-quoted POST /users emitted a route symbol. So double quotes drop match and resource routes too, not only get/post.\nDrift: the route marker's kind slot is now `function` (meta.framework_role=route), not `:route` as the repro output in the description shows.\nChokepoint answer to the item's question: _php_string_value (php.py:499) reads the first `string_content` child, which an encapsed_string also has; the call site at :803 bypasses it by its type test. _extract_controller_action already accepts encapsed_string (:591 array-action arm, marked `# pragma: no cover` = untested; :607 'C@a' arm). _laravel_collect_string_args/_laravel_extract_strings (:714, only/except) already accept both.\nSame-literal-type sweep, one more site: _laravel_match_methods (php.py:541) accepts only `string` for the verb array, so Route::match([\"get\",\"post\"], ...) degrades to the MATCH aggregate (degrades, not dropped).\nDesign point the fix must decide: an interpolated path \"/u/{$x}\" is an encapsed_string with variable children; _php_string_value would return only its first string_content (\"/u/\"), a truncated path. Refuse or mark such a path; do not emit the prefix as the route.\nNot checked: frequency on a real Laravel corpus repo."  # 2d26
- op: update  # f98f
