  set:  # f98f
    title: "php: double-quoted Laravel route paths silently undetected for every Route:: verb incl. match/resource (encapsed_string vs string); interpolated paths must be refused"  # f98f
    description: "php.py `_extract_laravel_routes` reads the route path only from a tree-sitter `string` node (php.py:803, `arg_child.type == \"string\"`) and never from `encapsed_string`, so every DOUBLE-QUOTED Laravel route path is silently undetected, for every Route:: verb including `match` and `resource`. Single quotes work.\n\nLive repro (re-run 2026-09-30), analyze_php on a scratch routes.php:\n\n    <?php\n    Route::get(\"/users\", [UserController::class, \"index\"]);            // NOT detected\n    Route::post('/users', [UserController::class, 'store']);           // detected\n    Route::match(['get','post'], \"/m\", [UserController::class, 'm']);  // NOT detected\n    Route::resource(\"photos\", PhotoController::class);                 // NOT detected\n    Route::get(\"/u/{$x}\", [UserController::class, 'i']);               // NOT detected\n\n  symbols: the file node, and one route marker\n    php:routes.php:3-3:POST /users:function  (meta.framework_role=route, controller_action UserController@store)\n\nParse tree confirms the cause: a double-quoted PHP literal is `encapsed_string` (children: `\"`, `string_content`, `\"`), a single-quoted one is `string`. The arg walk falls through on `encapsed_string`.\n\nDouble-quoted paths are idiomatic and common in Laravel, so this is a real route-detection coverage hole (WI-tosul family), not a cosmetic one. Same class of defect as WI-zunal's `Route::match` drop: an unsupported literal shape silently drops the whole route rather than degrading it.\n\nWHERE THE OTHER ARG WALKS STAND:\n- `_php_string_value` (php.py:499) reads the first `string_content` child, which an `encapsed_string` also has; the path site at :803 bypasses it by its type test. This is the chokepoint fix.\n- `_extract_controller_action` already accepts `encapsed_string` (array-action arm php.py:591, marked `# pragma: no cover`, i.e. untested; 'Controller@action' arm :607).\n- `_laravel_collect_string_args` / `_laravel_extract_strings` (only/except, :714) already accept both.\n- `_laravel_match_methods` (php.py:541) accepts only `string` in the verb array, so `Route::match([\"get\",\"post\"], ...)` degrades to the `MATCH` aggregate (degraded, not dropped). Fix it in the same change.\n\nINTERPOLATED PATHS MUST BE REFUSED, NOT TRUNCATED. `\"/u/{$x}\"` is an `encapsed_string` with variable children; `_php_string_value` would return only its first `string_content` (`/u/`). Emitting that prefix as the route would be a wrong route; accept an `encapsed_string` only when its children are plain `string_content` (and escapes), otherwise refuse or mark the path as dynamic.\n\nNot measured: frequency on a real Laravel corpus repo.\n\nFound while building route-parity fixtures for WI-zugob (the php fixture emitted zero markers, which is what surfaced it).\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # f98f
